  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The number of given orbitals which have electron density along the axis is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>xy</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>yz</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>xz</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The orbitals oriented along axis have electron density along the axis.</p><p>Orientation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math>&nbsp;orbitals are as follows:<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0075_2c1e981bfd3c.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 365px;\" /></p><p>Orientation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mo>:</mo></math><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0075_e28b6bac6659.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 310px;\" />,&nbsp;<br /><br />Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub></math> are axial orbitals.</p><p>The orbitals&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>xy</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>yz</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>xz</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;are oriented between the axis.</p>"
  }
}